          "id": "1777913954982",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777913954983_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Variables\n\nNodes: {{$context.$nodes.POST_PROCESS_FETCH_REFERENCED.$output.result.newNodes}} \n\n# Task\n\nFor each node in nodes:\n\n| Field | Value |\n| -------- | -------- | \n| code | node.code | \n| BusinessObjectCode | node.BusinessObjectCode | \n| FunctionName | node.FunctionName |\n| businessObjectsFunction | node.businessObjectsFunction |\n| paramaterMapping | See \"parametersMapping\" section below | \n| referenceRelationships | See \"referenceRelationships\" section below |\n\n\n## parametersMapping\n\nForeach item in node.businessObjectsFunction.InputParmeters:\n - return If there exists a referenceRelationships for this input, return {param_name: <InputParmeter name attribute>, name: null, code: null, type: <InputParmeter type>, value: null, source: node,  mainParameterSource: <See mainParameterSource section>}.\n - return {param_name: <InputParmeter name attribute>, name: null, code: null, type: <InputParmeter type>, value: null, source: null,  mainParameterSource: <See mainParameterSource section>}.\n\n### mainParameterSource\n\nTo calculate mainParameterSource, for each InputParmeter \"Sources\" attribute, examine the entries for possible sources for this parameter and determine best fit, and set  mainParameterSource to that entry.\n\n\n## referenceRelationships\n\nForeach ReferenceRelationship of businessObjectsFunction.ReferenceRelationships, assess using node.characteristic whether the given ReferenceRelationship needs to be used to fulfill the users' request. RelationshipAttributes is the attributes that are used to fetched the given relationship. If alwaysPresent is true, this relationship is required. Return minimum needed ReferenceRelationship."
